tests/isla/m7-traces.sh traces the Thumb forms of LeanExe/M7/Machine.lean from armv9p4-t32.ir, which
this diff makes from armv9p4-checked.ir, armv9p4.ir with tests/isla/armv9p4-checked.diff applied.
The diff edits the clause of __DecodeT32 that decodes B T3 and appends two harness functions, and
changes nothing else.

The decode of B T3 tests ConditionPassed(), which reads __currentCond, and uses the cond field of
its opcode only to send 1111 and 111x to other encodings (instrs32.sail 1463-1476).  Arm's ASL
declares AArch32.CurrentCond without defining it, and the Sail model's fetch loop sets
__currentCond to __DefaultCond, AL outside an IT block (fetch.sail 299), so the unedited model
branches on every B<cond>.W outside an IT block.  CurrentCond() of DDI 0403E.e A7.3.1 returns the
cond field of the encoding for the T1 and T3 encodings of B.  The first two hunks edit the clause
of __DecodeT32 for B T3 (instrs32.sail 1478-1487): after the statement that binds cond to bits 25
to 22 of the opcode (1481), a new statement writes cond to __currentCond, so that the decode's
ConditionPassed() tests the encoding's condition.  So that every statement keeps the index that
the jumps of __DecodeT32 name, the edit removes the earlier statement that assigns () to zz435240,
the unit result of SEE = 2854 (1479), which no statement reads, and no jump names an index between
the two.  A trace from the edited IR describes the M-profile's B T3 under the reading of A7.3.1
that its condition is the cond field.

The last hunk appends isla_footprint_t32 for a 32-bit opcode and isla_footprint_t16 for a 16-bit
one.  Each does what isla_footprint_no_init and isla_footprint_common do for an A64 opcode
(isla_main.sail 51-73): it runs InitFeatureImpl, sets SEE to -1 and DBGEN to Signal_Low, runs
Isla's reset, sets __ThisInstr and __ThisInstrEnc, and marks the start of the trace with
check_cycle_count.  It then sets __currentCond to __DefaultCond, as __InstructionExecute does
through __SetThisInstrDetails (fetch.sail 299), and calls __DecodeExecute (fetch.sail 250), which
decodes and executes the instruction through ExecuteT32__1 or ExecuteT16 and retries the decode
once after an SEE exception.  Around that call it keeps the handler of armv9p4-checked.ir:
Error_ExceptionTaken ends the path normally, and every other exception fails a Sail assertion,
which ends Isla's run with an error.  The write of __currentCond follows the cycle event, so a
trace records it, while Isla drops the writes that come before it.  Apply with
`cp armv9p4-checked.ir armv9p4-t32.ir && patch armv9p4-t32.ir < armv9p4-t32.diff`.

